cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "B.I.R.D.S — Broad Igneous Rocks: Diagrams & Statistics"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it together with the primary
  sources of the diagrams you used. Those are printed in each plot's
  subtitle and listed in full under References → Show full bibliography.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Darío
    family-names: Torres Sánchez
abstract: >-
  A desktop application for plotting, classifying and analysing
  whole-rock geochemical data of igneous rocks. Bundles 62 diagram
  templates (classification, tectonic discrimination, spider,
  petrographic ternaries and isotope systematics), 28 published
  normalisers including Ni-Cu-PGE metal references, the classical
  CIPW norm and an eight-tab statistics dashboard, with journal-ready
  figure export and reproducible session files.
keywords:
  - igneous petrology
  - geochemistry
  - whole-rock analysis
  - tectonic discrimination
  - classification diagrams
  - CIPW norm
  - spider diagram
  - REE
  - Ni-Cu-PGE
  - platinum-group elements
  - PySide6
version: 0.1.0b1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/DarioTorresSanchez/BIRDS"
url: "https://github.com/DarioTorresSanchez/BIRDS"
